    "q-224264": {
      "dom_id": "step-q224264",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "${700}^{2}=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate ${700}^{2},$ we start by writing it out with a multiplication sign:\n\n$$\n{700}^{2}={{700\\times 700}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{ times}}\n$$\n\nThen, we work out $700\\times 700.$\n\nFirst, we figure out the non-zero part and the block of zeros for both numbers:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}700 & \\,⟶\\,700 \\\\ 700 & \\,⟶\\,700\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can see that there are $4$ zeros in total.\n\nNext, we multiply the non-zero parts:\n\n$$\n7\\times 7=49\n$$\n\nFinally, we join the above with the block of zeros: \n\n$$\n490000=490,000\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${700}^{2}=490,000.$",
